Z||000016||California Kid||10-03-2001||08:23 PM||||Here's a couple rear view pics. Someone did a nice job on the one above by adding the upper rib.  What I plan to do with mine, when I have the time, is add an aluminium "wicker strip" around the upper side surface (fastening into the narrow vertical flat). It will resemble the original IMSA spoiler and set 1 to 1 1/2 inches higher that than the highest plane on the spoiler. May go with yellow anodize and black fasteners.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Tires_1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Post_GT_Rear_1.jpg"> <BR>Anyone going with this whale tail must follow install instructions very close. One of the things you have to do is remove at least 1/8 inch from all the interfacing edges of your original deck lid, so that it will fit properly, another is sand the underside outboard radius so it doesn't hit the quarter panel.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_7.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Bigfieroman||10-03-2001||09:25 PM||||Where can I get one?<P>------------------<BR>87 GT Automatic, Beretta GTZ Wheels, Kuhmo Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Poly cradle bushings.<BR>Future mods: Complete suspension redux w/anti-bumpsteer, all poly, rear swaybar, KYBs, Ground Control Coilovers, Street Dreams lowering spindles, plus exterior redux, w/window and quater panel scoops, Kid Danger air dam, 1fst2m6 style hood vent, 7" taller wing stantions, and black w/ silver racing stripes paint.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic_5.JPG">   <P>3800 S/C after all that!||||reg||1
