Z||000019||LZeitgeist||10-04-2001||07:52 AM||||&lt;bleah&gt; Not my cup of tea... glad you found what you've been hunting for, though! Congrats!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show||||reg||1
Z||000020||California Kid||10-04-2001||08:12 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>California Kid--Wanna run that by me again?  Shave 1/8" off of what?  And do what to the outboard what?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>The outer end of the Deck lid must be removed so the tail extension fits properly, the new extension is now the outer edge of your deck lid. Explained with pictures on instrution sheet, it's no big deal, just make sure you do all your (fittings) to check appearance before you bond it to the deck lid.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000021||ChopTop||10-04-2001||08:14 AM||||Should have mentioned one other thing, if your car didn't come with an original wing you may have to change the position of the tension rods to handle the additional weight, or you can install one of those aftermarket lifting rods.  Trust me, you don't want this sucker slamming down on your head.||||reg||1
